            <div xml:id="d1157">

                <pb facs="1197" n="1185" sameAs="frus:frus1945v08/pg1185"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/12–2145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Lebanon</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mattison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-21T16:00:00+02:00">December 21,
                            1945—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 228:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>427. British Legation informs me that full text of Anglo-French agreement will be
                    released in London and Paris at 3 p.m. GMT and that they are now issuing a local
                    communiqué announcing that talks between British and French military experts
                    began today.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Paris as 108, to London as 15. Sent to Department as 427.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mattison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
